sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Citizen as Citizen (Mobile App)
    participant Backend as Spring Boot Backend (:8080)
    participant Storage as File Storage Service (/uploads/)
    participant ML as Flask ML Service (:5001)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database (:5432)
    participant FCM as Firebase Cloud Messaging
    actor Supervisor as Municipal Supervisor
    actor Worker as Field Worker

    Note over Citizen,Backend: 1. Duplicate Check & Issue Submission
    Citizen->>Backend: POST /api/complaints/check-duplicates (coords, issueType)
    Backend->>DB: Query candidates by issueType & Haversine formula
    DB-->>Backend: Existing nearby complaints
    Backend-->>Citizen: 200 OK (matches list, distance, eligibleForJoin)

    alt Duplicate found & Citizen joins
        Citizen->>Backend: POST /api/complaints/{id}/join
        Backend->>DB: Insert into complaint_participants
        Backend-->>Citizen: 200 OK (joinCount, alreadyJoined)
    else New complaint creation
        Citizen->>Backend: POST /api/complaints/upload-image (Multipart file)
        Backend->>Storage: Store image (UUID.jpg)
        Storage-->>Backend: /uploads/uuid.jpg
        Backend-->>Citizen: 200 OK (imageUrl)

        Citizen->>Backend: POST /api/complaints (imageUrl, lat, lon, issueType)
        Backend->>DB: Insert complaint (status=SUBMITTED, SLA deadline)
        Backend->>DB: Insert status_history ('Complaint submitted by citizen')
        Backend->>FCM: Async send 'Complaint submitted successfully'

        Note over Backend,ML: 2. Automated Two-Stage ML Triage
        Backend->>ML: POST /predict (Multipart image bytes)
        ML->>ML: Stage 1: Binary filter (urbanpulse_binary_v2_best.keras)
        alt Non-Civic Image (not_civic_prob >= 0.50)
            ML-->>Backend: JSON (isCivic=false, NOT_CIVIC_ISSUE)
            Backend->>DB: Update status=REJECTED, assignment=REJECTED_NON_CIVIC_IMAGE
        else Confirmed Civic Issue (not_civic_prob < 0.50)
            ML->>ML: Stage 2: 8-Class classifier (urbanpulse_8class_pothole_stage1.keras)
            ML-->>Backend: JSON (predictedClass, confidence, probabilities)
            alt Confidence > 0.50 & Department/Supervisor exists
                Backend->>DB: Update status=FORWARDED, assignment=AUTO_ML, set supervisor
                Backend->>FCM: Notify citizen & supervisor
            else Confidence <= 0.50 or missing supervisor
                Backend->>DB: Update status=SUBMITTED, requiresManualReview=true
            end
        end
        Backend-->>Citizen: 201 Created (ComplaintResponse)
    end

    Note over Supervisor,Worker: 3. Worker Dispatch & Remediation
    Supervisor->>Backend: PATCH /api/supervisor/complaints/{id}/assign-worker (workerMobile)
    Backend->>DB: Update status=ASSIGNED, assigned_worker
    Backend->>FCM: Notify worker & citizen(s)

    Worker->>Backend: PATCH /api/worker/complaints/{id}/status (status=IN_PROGRESS)
    Backend->>DB: Update status=IN_PROGRESS
    Backend->>FCM: Notify citizen(s)

    Worker->>Backend: POST /api/worker/complaints/{id}/proof (Multipart proof photo)
    Backend->>Storage: Store proof image
    Backend->>DB: Update proof_image_url

    Worker->>Backend: PATCH /api/worker/complaints/{id}/status (status=RESOLVED)
    Backend->>DB: Update status=RESOLVED, resolved_at=now(), resolved_within_sla
    Backend->>FCM: Notify all joined citizens ('Complaint resolved')
